INVALID_HISTORY_QUERY
Usage: node scripts/prepare-portfolio-history.js combine DAT|EMA|CAWELON first.json [more.json ...]
       node scripts/prepare-portfolio-history.js prune history.json [filters]
Combine: 1-16 archives, each <= 1 MiB, total <= 4 MiB, at most 64 unique observations.
Prune filters: --account ADDRESS --chain ID --origin ORIGIN --min-block N --max-block N
               --token CONTRACT --token-state any|known|unknown|not-observed --order oldest|newest
Prune prepares the complement of an explicit nonempty proper subset; order alone is not a scope.
OUTPUT ONLY: writes a candidate history JSON to stdout. Never deletes, overwrites or imports any file or live history.
Review the candidate before importing. Keep the original files for recovery. Output includes public addresses and balances.
Exit 0: complete local candidate; 1: rejected arguments, input, conflict, capacity or scope. No partial stdout on failure.
No network or wallet access. Structural agreement is not authentication, current balance verification or a security audit.
